SlothClash core patch 0044: finalmask on vless and trojan.

Xray-core's finalmask (streamSettings.finalmask) as a finalmask block on
vless and trojan proxies and inbounds: a chain of masks between the socket
and TLS / REALITY, written as in Xray (first entry outermost, settings
nesting optional). tcp: header-custom, fragment (on component/fragment,
0032), sudoku, xmc. udp: noise, header-custom, sudoku, udphop, xdns, used
only by vless over xhttp with alpn [h3]. Xray's camelCase keys (maxSplit,
randRange) are read as the kebab-case option names at every depth, so a
block copied from Xray JSON or a panel decodes completely.

Masks open their sockets through the proxy's dialer, so interface binding,
routing marks and dialer-proxy apply. A block that cannot be used (bad
option, unknown mask, UDP masks on another network, any mask on xdrive,
xicmp) does not fail the profile, as with 0043: the proxy loads, the core
logs "unusable finalmask, the proxy will not connect", and every dial fails
(finalmask.Broken), so the node never goes out without its masks.

xicmp is refused on every platform: it opens its ICMP sockets itself, not
through the dialer, so with TUN and auto-route its echo requests would enter
the core's own tunnel. xdrive (0004) dials a storage service that cannot
take masks off, so a block there is unusable and the xdrive dial checks it.

Ported from Prizrak-Core v1.19.34-r4.
Adapted to this series: component/fragment instead of its fragment
transport, the trojan listener hunk on 0040, graceful errors, the xicmp
refusal and the xdrive rule. Xray-core code keeps its MPL-2.0 notices.
Not ported: mKCP with the UDP chain, xdns DoH resolvers, the utls-fork
interop test. Delete when mihomo ships finalmask.

Tests: transport/finalmask/... (every mask, the registry, camelCase keys,
xicmp refused), adapter (parse; unusable, xicmp and xdrive blocks load and
fail their dials), adapter/outbound, listener/inbound (loopback client and
inbound with the same chains), config (a profile with valid blocks loads
with working chains; unusable blocks keep it loading). The Xray interop test
in adapter is skipped without XRAY_BINARY.

